  "slug": "proteomic-plasma-ea4b",
  "summary": "Multi-dataset transcriptomic pipelines paired with machine learning and docking are producing a steady stream of candidate biomarkers and targets.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational prioritization of hub genes or candidate compounds from public transcriptomic, single-cell or network data. Most items pair differential expression or WGCNA with machine learning, and several add Mendelian randomization, molecular docking or molecular dynamics. Experimental support is generally limited and varies: the Parkinson's study reports partial validation, and the LILRB3 study adds DSS-mouse and macrophage knockdown experiments. Novelty lies mainly in biological context, including oxidative stress-associated gene signatures in myositis, FOS as an epithelial-associated candidate in chronic atrophic gastritis, and the sulforaphane preprint's docking of 693 targets against neurodegeneration-linked transcriptomic data. Several entries, such as the gut-lung microbial metabolite network and the methionine metabolism signature in chronic rhinosinusitis, extend the same omics-plus-learning logic to metabolic axes.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-31"
}
